  "summary": "Berkeley police arrested a man suspected of stealing $2,400 in coats from a North Face outlet after a Flock ALPR alert flagged his Toyota Corolla returning to the city the next day. Officers stopped the suspect, who was wearing a stolen jacket, and recovered additional merchandise, drugs, and stolen financial items.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Less than 24 hours later, Monday at 1 p.m., police got a license plate alert from the city's Flock camera system that the Corolla was back in Berkeley near Ninth and Gilman streets.",
